module

public import Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30StripCertificates
public import Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30PeriodTwoCoupled

/-!
# A trap for the gate of the alternating-driven right half: data and kernel checks

Data for `Rule30GateTrap`. A *window* is the list of the colors of the columns `1..16` of a right
half driven by the alternating column (`Rule30PeriodTwoCoupled.altCol`), at an odd time. It is coded
as a `16`-bit number, bit `i` being column `i + 1` (`decode`). From an odd time, column `0` is
white, then black, so two steps after the window `w` the window is `step2 w x1 x2`, where `x1` and
`x2` are the two values of column `17`, which the window does not determine.

* `trap`: `829` windows such that `step2 w x1 x2` is again in `trap` for every `w` in `trap` and all
  `x1`, `x2` (`trapClosed_ok`).
* `layer1` … `layer4`: the windows that follow a black cell of column `1`. Two steps after a window
  of `trap` whose column `1` is black, column `1` is white, and white again two steps later; two
  steps after that it is black (a gap of `3`), or white, then white, then black (a gap of `5`)
  (`afterBlack_ok`, `secondStep_ok`, `thirdStep_ok`, `fourthStep_ok`, `fifthStep_ok`).
* `entryCode`: the window of the empty right half at time `293`, computed from the white row
  (`evolve_293`); it is in `trap` (`entry_mem`).

Each check is decided by the kernel (`decide +kernel`).
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30GateTrap

open Rule30StripCertificates Rule30PeriodTwoCoupled

